# charon integration step 53 after 546078ea5d: commit d5ba232f0bba63ad7e6a898976399cf8dadf81a6
# first parent b947e944415f15a3a726b96a093e5560fb73ff0f
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon-ml: the name-matcher lexer reads multi-digit integer literals
#
# The lexer produced one INT token per digit, so a pattern with a
# multi-digit array length, const generic value or disambiguator
# (`[@T; 32]`, `ArrayToSliceShared<'_, bool, 32>`, `f#12`) failed with
# "Parse error" (Aeneas: "Could not parse pattern"), although the printer
# emits such literals with TkPattern. `digit+` lexes the whole literal.
#
# Tests: charon-ml int_literal_tests (parse, structure and print round trip
# of multi-digit literals) and ml-name-matcher-tests.rs cases matching an
# impl for [T; 32] and an ArrayToSliceShared call with length 32 (the
# patterns with 3 and 320 fail). The Rust pattern parser already reads
# multi-digit disambiguators and has no array syntax.

